diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4dec6d5e..5a52f5ac 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -65,6 +65,8 @@ F11’s scene picker exposes native prototypes in all 18 levels: six LN1, seven
 
 On a phone or tablet an on-screen overlay appears: a black C64-style joystick on the left (eight directions), and two red buttons on the right, **FIRE** (the # fire key) and **SPACE** (next weapon), so moving and attacking work with two thumbs. Along the bottom, **MUSIC**, **ITEM >**, **< ITEM**, **PAUSE**, **< WEAPON**, **CRT** and **SAVE** do the same as F1, F3, F5, F7, the previous-weapon trigger, F9 and Ctrl+S; **KEYS** hides or shows that row while the joystick and buttons stay. **ESC** (top-left, or the Android Back button) closes an open panel, and otherwise asks whether to quit. Menus, save slots and the toolbar respond to taps directly. With the UI hidden, double-tap the top of the screen to bring it back.
 
+Pinch with two fingers to zoom in on any screen, up to 3x (never smaller than full screen), and move both fingers to pan. A double tap anywhere resets the zoom. Fingers on the joystick, FIRE, SPACE, the key row, ESC or TOUCH never zoom, so play continues normally while zoomed, and the overlay stays where it is. Taps on menus and buttons follow the zoom. Settings, ARRANGE and the quit prompt always open at full size.
+
 **TOUCH** (top-right) opens settings: controls on/off, button size, opacity, the key row and **Game size**. **ARRANGE** lets you drag the joystick, FIRE and SPACE anywhere; RESET puts them back. Game size enlarges the picture when the UI is hidden: 100% (3x C64 pixels), 133% (4x) or 167% (5x, the largest that fits). Whole C64 pixels keep every CRT scanline the same height. Settings are saved in the `[Touch]` section of `LNPreserve.ini`. On Android and iOS all button and label text uses Roboto Medium (included under `datafiles/fonts` with its Apache 2.0 licence) instead of Jansina. For testing on Windows or macOS with the mouse, set `desktop=1` in `[Touch]`; `clear_font=1` uses Roboto there too.
 
 ## Verification
